    title: "Go-To-Market Consultant vs Marketing Agency: Which One Do You Need?",
    excerpt: "A go-to-market consultant defines strategy: ideal customer profile, positioning, pricing, channel selection, and messaging architecture. A marketing agency executes demand: campaigns, creative, media buying, and content production at volume. Companies that buy execution before strategy typically pay twice, once for the wrong campaigns, again for the rebuild.",
    readTime: "13 min read",
